From 3f896af60c909826a0096c299d6366f580667a61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moWerk <mo@mowerk.net>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:01:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 38/40] cpuidle: psci: Initialize after the deferred probes.
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The psci-cpuidle faux device probes once, at device_initcall. With the
MPM as the parent of both CPU cluster domains, the PSCI domains defer
until the MPM probes and arrive only from the deferred probe work. So
the cpuidle driver found no domain ("CPU 0 failed to PSCI idle") and
the CPUs only ever ran WFI. late_initcall_sync comes after
deferred_probe_initcall has run and flushed them.

Taken from the Lenovo TB-J606L (SM6115) port: haltia-de/device-lenovo-tb-j606l
kernel patch 0017, with its MPM device tree (next commit).

Disclosure: LLMGD-2 · origin O1 (the model took the J606L port's patch; built and running on the device)
LLMGD: v0.3; assurance=A2; flags=T; origin=O1; origin_headline=O1; scope=kernel; graded-by=model; retrieval=none
---
 drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
index b250d0dde..0ad6669c8 100644
--- a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
+++ b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
@@ -479,4 +479,9 @@ static int __init psci_idle_init(void)
 
 	return 0;
 }
-device_initcall(psci_idle_init);
+/*
+ * The faux device probes once. The CPU PM domains may still wait for a
+ * parent domain (the MPM on SM6115 and QCM2290) and come only from the
+ * deferred probes, which late_initcall runs and waits for.
+ */
+late_initcall_sync(psci_idle_init);
